%% Anchor / pruning rollup — sequence
%% See docs/02-layer2-anchor.md §3 and ADR-0001
sequenceDiagram
    participant DAG as L1 BlockDAG (events)
    participant Pruner as ZK Pruning Prover
    participant Anchor as Anchor Proposer
    participant L2 as Base L2: IKeychainAnchor
    participant ETH as Ethereum L1 (settlement)

    Note over DAG: Events accumulate for the epoch
    DAG->>Pruner: epoch boundary triggers proof
    Pruner-->>Pruner: build Merkle accumulator
    Pruner-->>Pruner: generate ZK proof of correct summarization
    Pruner->>Anchor: dagStateRoot + zkProof
    Anchor->>L2: commitEpoch(root, proof, epoch)
    L2-->>L2: verifyZkProof(...)
    L2-->>L2: store root by epoch
    L2-->>DAG: emit EpochAnchored
    Note over DAG: After 30 days, pre-epoch events can be pruned;<br/>users retain copies on StorageNet
    L2-->>ETH: included in next L2 batch
    ETH-->>L2: L2 finality after challenge window
    Note over L2,ETH: Optimistic L2 finality lags ~7d;<br/>protocol-level finality is at commitEpoch ack
